# The constructor is inlined and its two assignments to this are the first values of the cell: one allocation, two stores of unboxed doubles.
# The function is split in two: this half allocates, for callers that need the object. The other half computes the fields.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWrapper
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Double, Double b@[[fields]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[x]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<0,
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[y]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<1,
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[point]] = Patchpoint($1(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[x]], b@[[point]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[y]], b@[[point]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK: Return(b@[[point]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Nothing reads the class, its prototype or new.target, nothing fills the fields with a placeholder first, and the constructor is not called.
# NONE-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWrapper
# NONE-NOT: Reads:ModuleVariables
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-NOT: |Writes:JSCell_header
# NONE-NOT: :PutSlot
# NONE-COUNT-2: Store(
# NONE-NOT: Store(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# The half that computes the fields allocates nothing.
# NONE-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWorker
# NONE-NOT: :NewObject
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
